/target
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store

# Anything derived from the private document archive lives here and never
# leaves this machine: the labelled token dataset, extracted document text,
# and any intermediate file that could carry a phrase from a real document.
# Only aggregate statistics may be committed, and never from this directory.
/local/

# The studio's working memory. Local to this machine, never shipped.
/Dev-Memory/


# The project-local build environment: its own Rust compiler and package cache.
# Several gigabytes, entirely rebuildable, and specific to this machine. The
# files that DEFINE it — rust-toolchain.toml, deny.toml, .sandbox/activate — are
# committed; the downloaded contents are not.
#
# `corpus-paths.local` is excluded on purpose and must stay excluded: it names the
# folders holding the private document archive, and those folder names are
# themselves the sort of thing this project has already had to scrub from commit
# messages once.
/.sandbox/*
!/.sandbox/activate

# Claude Code's per-machine settings, which hold absolute local paths.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Fuzzing artefacts: generated inputs and crash cases, some derived from real
# documents. The fuzz targets themselves are source and ARE committed.
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/target/

# Third-party vendor material, supplied for analysis and NEVER redistributable.
#
# The Bijoy fonts are commercial products of their vendor and the typing guide is
# their copyrighted documentation. This repository is public and MIT-licensed, so
# committing any of it would be a licence violation — a much larger one than the
# private-document trap LESSONS §14 records, because it is somebody else's
# property rather than the owner's own.
#
# What this project may legitimately take from them is **facts about the
# encoding** — which byte means which character — and those live in
# crates/mukti-core/src/tables.rs with their evidence written beside them.
# Nothing here is needed to build, test or measure Mukti.
# Named by pattern rather than by title, so the ignore list does not itself
# catalogue which of the vendor's materials happen to be on this machine.
*.zip
*.webarchive
Bijoy*/
Bijoy*.pdf
